      <section class="section-insight for-whom">
        <div class="w-layout-blockcontainer container-1408 horizontal w-container">
          <div class="column-wrapper">
            <div class="top_side-slider-2 left center-sm">
              <div class="gap-4-purpose">
                <div class="text-12-caps-2 opacity-60">WHAT WE LEARNED</div>
                <div class="max-w-380-slider full">
                  <h2 class="h2"><span class="span-pink-2">Most people struggle to understand</span> <br>unfamiliar health information</h2>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="text-16-150-3 opacity-80">The challenge is not only medical terminology. People may be worried, distracted, or making an unfamiliar decision, so every explanation needs to be clear without becoming incomplete.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="w-layout-vflex list-wrap">
              <div class="card-2">
                <div class="card-content-why_choose-3 direction-horizontal padding-tight"><img loading="lazy" src="/images/Key-Insight-Icon---01.avif" alt="A purple circle with a play button on it" class="img-why_choose">
                  <div class="text-14-150-3 opacity-80">Only 12% of US adults have the health literacy to fully understand and act on health information, meaning nearly 9 in 10 people will struggle with at least part of what your product tells them (HHS National Assessment of Adult Literacy).<br></div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="card-2">
                <div class="card-content-why_choose-3 direction-horizontal padding-tight"><img loading="lazy" src="/images/Key-Insight-Icon---02.avif" alt="A purple button with a blue envelope on it" class="img-why_choose">
                  <div class="text-14-150-3 opacity-80">Patients immediately forget 40 to 80% of the medical information they&#x27;re given, and about half of what they do remember, they remember wrong (Journal of the Royal Society of Medicine).<br></div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="card-2">
                <div class="card-content-why_choose-3 direction-horizontal padding-tight"><img loading="lazy" src="/images/Key-Insight-Icon---03.avif" alt="A purple button with a speaker inside of it" class="img-why_choose">
                  <div class="text-14-150-3 opacity-80">Understanding tracks education closely, people without a high school diploma recall around 38% of care recommendations, against 65% for college graduates, so clear content can&#x27;t assume a well-read audience (Endocrinology Advisor).<br></div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="card-2">
                <div class="card-content-why_choose-3 direction-horizontal padding-tight"><img loading="lazy" src="/images/Key-Insight-Icon---04.avif" alt="A purple button with a shopping cart on it" class="img-why_choose">
                  <div class="text-14-150-3 opacity-80">Patient education videos rated highly understandable earn significantly more views, likes, and comments than harder-to-follow ones, which makes plain language a reach strategy, not just a courtesy (JMIR).</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="column-wrapper hide-small"><img loading="lazy" src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/67601fee10470581a90722d7/67602bd27d29b464069f8f7a_Key%20Insight.png" alt=""></div>
        </div>
      </section>
